---
// THE FULL-SIZE VIEWER — one dialog for the whole page, opened by any control
// that carries a `data-zoom-src`.
//
// ONE DIALOG, NOT ONE PER IMAGE. The gallery renders every shot up front
// because choosing between them must be instant; this is the opposite case.
// It opens on a deliberate gesture, one image at a time, and the bytes it wants
// are the bytes already on the page — so a single `<img>` with a swapped `src`
// costs a cache hit rather than a request, and eight hidden dialogs would be
// eight copies of markup to keep in step for no gain.
//
// WHAT IT SHOWS IS THE ASSET, WHOLE. `contain`, never `cover`: the gallery
// crops to fill its field and this is the control that undoes that. A zoom that
// showed the same crop larger would answer a question nobody asked — the
// operator's framing is visible everywhere else on the page.
//
// `<dialog>` AND `showModal()` CARRY THE HARD PARTS. Focus moves in and is
// trapped, `Esc` closes, the rest of the page goes inert, and the backdrop is a
// real pseudo-element rather than a div pretending. `<form method="dialog">`
// closes without script at all, so the close button works even if the handler
// that opened it has since thrown.
//
// THE PLATE IS FOR LINE ART. A size chart is dark ink on transparency — over
// the dialog's own dark ground it would be invisible, and it is the one image
// here that is NOT a photograph. `on-plate` paints white behind it. The shop
// tints the same file to the page's ink with a mask; at full size that would be
// a silhouette of a chart rather than a chart, so this shows it as drawn.
---

<dialog class="product-zoom" data-zoom aria-label="Full-size image">
  {/*
    A form rather than a click handler: `method="dialog"` closes the dialog as
    a platform behaviour, with no JavaScript of ours in the path.
  */}
  <form method="dialog">
    <button type="submit" class="product-zoom-close" aria-label="Close">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M3 3 13 13 M13 3 3 13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></path>
      </svg>
    </button>
  </form>

  {/*
    `alt` is set from whatever opened this, so the description a screen reader
    gets at full size is the one the operator wrote for that image — not a
    second, emptier one belonging to the viewer.
  */}
  <img data-zoom-image src="" alt="" />
</dialog>
